{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the sliding window with the first four values:\n    # fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n    # Iterate from n=4 up to the desired n, updating the window\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_val = a + b + c + d\n        a, b, c, d = b, c, d, next_val\n        \n    return d"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import List, Any, Sequence, Iterable\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Indicate an invalid element in the input list.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str, index: int | None = None) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n        self.index = index\nclass EmptyListError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Indicate an empty input list.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Input list is empty\") -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\ndef _parse_number(value: Any) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Convert a value to float, handling int, float, and numeric strings.\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(value, (int, float)):\n        if isinstance(value, float) and (math.isinf(value) or math.isnan(value)):\n            raise ValueError(\"NaN or Infinity not allowed\")\n        return float(value)\n    if isinstance(value, str):\n        s = value.strip()\n        try:\n            f = float(s)\n        except ValueError:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Cannot parse '{value}' as number\")\n        if math.isinf(f) or math.isnan(f):\n            raise ValueError(\"NaN or Infinity not allowed\")\n        return f\n    raise ValueError(\"Unsupported type for numeric conversion\")\ndef _convert_and_validate_item(value: Any, index: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Convert a single item, raising InvalidInputError on failure.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return _parse_number(value)\n    except ValueError:\n        raise InvalidInputError(f\"Invalid numeric value at index {index}\", index=index)\ndef _validate_list(values: Iterable[Any]) -> List[float]:\n    \"\"\"Validate and convert all items in the list to floats.\"\"\"\n    result: List[float] = []\n    for i, v in enumerate(values):\n        val = _convert_and_validate_item(v, i)\n        result.append(val)\n    if not result:\n        raise EmptyListError()\n    return result\ndef _median_of_sorted(sorted_vals: List[float]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Compute the median of an already sorted list of floats.\"\"\"\n    n = len(sorted_vals)\n    mid = n // 2\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        return float(sorted_vals[mid])\n    return (float(sorted_vals[mid - 1]) + float(sorted_vals[mid])) / 2.0\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    normalized_list = _validate_list(l)\n    \n    nums_to_sort = list(normalized_list)\n    nums_to_sort.sort()\n    \n    return _median_of_sorted(nums_to_sort)"}
